From bee3d196037265b218d4ebd94c277db40611e4a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:13:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 68/68] software_isp: debayer_egl: Add lens shading correction

Add an optional lens shading stage to the GPU debayer. DebayerParams
carries a grid of up to 32x32 RGB gains spanning the sensor's active
area, and the part of it the image covers; the EGL debayer uploads the
grid as a texture and the fragment shaders multiply by the bilinearly
sampled gain after black level subtraction. With no grid, the stage is
an identity and costs one texture lookup.

The simple IPA's new Lsc algorithm fills the grid from the tuning file
and derives the covered part from the sensor's analogue crop, so binned
and cropped modes sample the right region. The CPU debayer does not
apply it.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
